WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:07.820 align:start position:0%
 
I  World of Tanks will change greatly in  2014 we've already told you about the  new physics and graphics that will  improve the beauty and atmosphere of the  game now let's talk about features that  will bring more diversity into battles  new game modes  it has been long known that the current  global map is not enough most provinces  are controlled by a number of top plans  for most glands it's almost impossible  to win a landing tournament and there is  not much to do on the global map but to  fight over the provinces something  needed to be done we developed a brand  new feature and called it fortification  we've decided that fortifications will  be given to all clans in the game there  will be a certain minimum number of clan  members for a clan to get its  fortification a clan with only one  player doesn't need a fortification  because this player won't be able to  defend it and their fortifications clans  will be able to construct buildings  different buildings will give different  economic bonuses to construct them plans  will need resources this is a new type  of currency and clans will have to fight  with each other to obtain it after each  type of building has been constructed  the so-called reserves will appear in  the fortification reserves will be like  small events for the clan that owns that  fortification for example combat pay  will give a ten percent bonus for  credits in every battle including random  battles for three or four hours bonuses  could be different there could be credit  bonuses or bonuses to experience or free  experience which bonuses are available  will depend on how clans develop their  fortifications in this game mode there  will be an enticing but fateful  opportunity clans will be able to not  only build fortifications but also to  ransack them to protect new clans from  more experienced and strong ones the  mode of attack and defense will be  available only when a fortification  reaches its fifth level of development  this new game mode will be independent  from the current global map  fortifications will have nothing to do  with it clam players can fight for their  fortifications and take part in battles  on the global map these are two  independent opportunities players can  fight in both game modes or they can  choose one they can choose neither at  all it depends on their preferences  fortifications will provide a number of  opportunities that are not available and  won't ever be available in other game  modes this is not only about managing  the fortification this is also an  opportune  you use brand new features on the  battlefield players will be able to call  in bombers conduct reconnaissance lay  mines or install pill boxes that will  perform the role of additional artillery  forces these features will diversify the  battles and make them more remarkable  and unique now players will not only  focus on their vehicles but also pay  attention to what's happening around  them basically fortifications will  create a parallel universe in World of  Tanks a game within the game work on  improving this game mode will continue  historical battle mode discussed almost  since the day the game was first  released will finally appear in the 9.0  update the main problem of historical  battles was to develop a good system of  vehicle matchmaking in real battles  tanks that fought against each other  differed greatly and their capabilities  for example the KD 1 and the t-34 with  76 millimeter guns fought against tigers  for quite a long time the powerful  German heavy tanks were overcome with  artillery air forces infantry and  landmines there are no such things in  the game so developers had to look for  other ways of balancing teams one of the  solutions is unequal team members this  means that one team may have 15 vehicles  while the other may have only 3 the  scheme was applied in the first version  of historical battles which was tested  on the common test servers it turned out  that this scheme was not sufficient to  balance the chances of the teams so we  had to make additional changes in  historical battle mode vehicles  specifications such as maneuverability  speed and view range will be different  from what they have in other game modes  probably most importantly the number of  hit points will change heavy vehicles  will be easier to destroy earlier in the  process we tested the prototype of  historical battle mode that did away  with vehicle hit points to destroy a  vehicle you had to knock out all of its  modules or put all of its crew members  out of action this approach made the  game worse we understood that players  would become frustrated  they didn't understand why they kept  firing at enemy tanks for a long time  but the enemy tank just wouldn't get  destroyed and other times the very same  vehicle might be destroyed with a single  shot sometimes we watch two tanks just  standing and firing at each other for  more than two minutes with no  consequences in the first minutes of the  battle vehicles usually had about half  of their modules knocked up after  several battles everyone realized that  the best tactic was to hide and wait  almost until the end of the battle and  then finish off the damaged vehicles  there's a third-party mod that displays  zones of penetration on the vehicle  model if we make this game mode too  realistic everyone might feel forced to  play with this mod however the next  variant of team matchmaking in  historical battles is about to be  released and that upcoming system each  team will have several main heavy  vehicles and a larger number of lighter  support vehicles for example one team  with a few Tigers and a larger number of  pz threes will fight a team with several  kV ones and larger numbers of T 46 s and  BTW sevens we need to make these battles  both playable and interesting to play to  do this we have developed and used of  prototype that allows these lighter  support tanks to respawn into the battle  sometime after they've been destroyed  now these tags will have the freedom to  make mistakes tests showed that these  lighter tanks will try to spot and  attack enemy forces more aggressively so  this respawn system sets the stage for  aggressive tank clashes historical  battles will be introduced as events  that will recreate the real episodes in  history such as the Battle of curse or  the battle of bulge players will be able  to join historical battle only in  vehicles that took part in that battle  in real life vehicles will automatically  be brought to their historical setups  even if you have not researched the  required modules yet players will not  have their choice of ammunition the  number of shells of different types will  be predetermined teams will be assembled  based on nationality for example German  and Soviet vehicles will be on opposite  teams for the Battle of curse everything  will correspond with the real events of  1943 t-34s against tigers and Panthers  the degree of realism in historic  battles is quite moderate consumables  and crew skills and perks even Sixth  Sense will be active playing this game  mode we don't want players to feel like  they're struggling with their own  vehicles they should fight and have fun  while getting the flavor of a historical  battle we want to communicate the  atmosphere of the battle by different  means and we don't want to deprive the  players of the key elements they enjoy  and are used to perhaps all vehicles  that participate in historical battles  will have a feature typical of premium  vehicles players will be able to  transfer their crews from vehicles of  the same type without penalty or  retraining historical battle mode is on  its way another game mode that is  planned for release closer to the end of  the year is garage battle mode in this  game mode players will be able to roll  out several vehicles one by one as they  get destroyed two variants are being  considered the first variant includes  tier 10 vehicles only the second one  allows vehicles of different tiers to  participate to play this game mode  players will need several vehicles of  the same type they will be able to  replenish ammunition and consumables  during the battle however it's too early  to tell exactly what garage battles will  look like details are still being worked  through and haven't been specified yet  along with the introduction of these  three game modes team battle mode will  also be improved in 2014 new features  are being developed to support long-term  teams new online tournaments and special  awards will be introduced the team  battle rules will be updated and many  other small but helpful features will be  introduced that's all for now in the  next episode of developer Diaries we  will tell you how maps will change in  2014 good luck on the battlefield  tankers  you

